# TypeScript conventions
<!-- EXAMPLE of an Auto-Attached rule. Duplicate this pattern per stack
     (30-python.mdc, 40-flutter.mdc, etc.) and delete what you don't use. -->

- `strict: true` semantics assumed. No `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing.
- Functional components + hooks only (no class components).
- Named exports; default exports only for framework-required files.
- Types co-located with usage; shared types in `src/types/`.
- Prefer `type` over `interface` unless declaration merging is required.
- Handle promise rejections explicitly — no floating promises.
